# CatDex — Git Workflow

Canonical doc: `docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md`.

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `main` | Production |
| `develop` | Integration |
| `feature/*`, `fix/*`, `hotfix/*`, `chore/*`, `docs/*` | Temporary |

PRs land in **`develop`** first; release to `main` separately. Hotfixes may target `main` with care.

## Commits

Conventional commits:

```
feat: … | fix: … | refactor: … | docs: … | test: … | chore: … | perf: … | ci: …
```

## Agent / Cloud notes

- Cloud agents may use `cursor/<name>-****` branches — still open a proper PR and avoid long-lived divergence
- Prefer updating PR description when scope changes
- Never force-push shared `main` / `develop`

## PR body

- Summary of product impact
- Test plan with checkboxes
- Note Vision/schema/env changes explicitly
